    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d498">

                <pb facs="1274" n="1124" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1124"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister of the
                        Netherlands.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-05-11"><hi rendition="#italic">May 11,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 134]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 7th instant, inclosing, by order of your Government, the
                    text of a protocol concerning the adhesion of States not represented at the
                    First Conference to the convention for the pacific settlement of international
                    disputes, and requesting that the American delegates to the Second Peace
                    Conference be supplied with full powers to sign the protocol at The Hague on
                    June 14.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that the President has issued his full
                    power authorizing the American delegates to sign the protocol for and in the
                    name of the United States.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
